  "sn22.60:2.2": "This view is attributed to the Bamboo-staffed Ascetic Gosāla, founder of the Ājīvakas, at <a href='https://suttacentral.net/dn2/en/sujato#20.2'>DN 2:20.2</a>. There, Pūraṇa Kassapa advocates the inefficacy of action (<a href='https://suttacentral.net/dn2/en/sujato#16.1'>DN 2:16.1</a>), while at <a href='https://suttacentral.net/sn46.56/en/sujato'>SN 46.56</a> he is said to teach that there is no cause for knowledge. ",
